From 839100f1b06e60b9dc6ad9faece125bdbd0d20c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 12:21:01 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hw/adc: U2247 conversion time, sequences, events, DMA and
 client ADC

The PIC32CM ADC now converts on a timer in the time PIC32CM MC00 silicon
takes (firmware/hello APP=adcprobe..adcprobe5, checked by adcseq): N x
(SAMPLEN + 1, or 4 with OFFCOMP, + the resolution's bits) + 1 CLK_ADC
cycles, N the averaged samples, after a start of 36 GCLK_ADC cycles; no
conversion starts within 10 us of the enable. SWTRIG.START reads 1
until the conversion starts. Free running converts back to back from
the enable; a sequence (SEQCTRL) converts its inputs from the lowest
with SEQSTATUS (SEQBUSY and the last input), repeating with FREERUN.

The START and SYNC (flush) event inputs act on their rising edge
(falling with STARTINV/FLUSHINV); a flush aborts the conversion in
progress and, free running or in a sequence, starts it again. RESRDY
and WINMON pulse their event outputs. RESRDY is a DMA request: the SoC
wires the ADC's DMAC_ID_RESRDY as a level trigger on INTFLAG, and the
ADC kicks the DMAC (new mchp_dmac_u2223_kick) so that a waiting channel
moves each result. ADC1 with CTRLA.SLAVEEN is ADC0's client: ADC0's
enable, starts and prescaler drive it, both converting at once
(DUALSEL BOTH) or in turn (INTERLEAVE).

Event input levels survive a SWRST in the ADC and the TCC: they are
lines, not registers.

qtest pic32cm-adc-test: timing, start-up, averaging, free running,
sequences, events, the client ADC.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
